  "content": {
    "id": "p37-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "The population of an ant colony is given by $P=950+Ae^{kt}$, where $t$ is measured in weeks. If there are initially 14000 ants and after 6 weeks there are 20000, find:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p37-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "the ant population after 10 weeks, to the nearest ant",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "25464 ants.",
          "worked": "At $t=0$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}14000&=950+A\\\\A&=13050\\end{aligned}$$\nAt $t=6$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}20000&=950+13050e^{6k}\\\\19050&=13050e^{6k}\\\\e^{6k}&=\\frac{19050}{13050}=\\frac{127}{87}\\\\k&=\\frac{1}{6}\\ln\\left(\\frac{127}{87}\\right)\\end{aligned}$$\nThus $P(t)=950+13050e^{kt}$. At $t=10$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}P(10)&=950+13050e^{10k}\\\\&=950+13050\\left(\\frac{127}{87}\\right)^{5/3}\\\\&\\approx25464\\end{aligned}$$\nThe population is approximately 25464 ants.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 47
      },
      {
        "id": "p37-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "when the population will reach 1 million, to 1 decimal place in weeks.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "After approximately 68.8 weeks.",
          "worked": "Using $P=950+13050e^{kt}$ with $k=\\frac{1}{6}\\ln\\left(\\frac{127}{87}\\right)$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}1000000&=950+13050e^{kt}\\\\999050&=13050e^{kt}\\\\e^{kt}&=\\frac{999050}{13050}\\\\kt&=\\ln\\left(\\frac{999050}{13050}\\right)\\\\t&=\\frac{\\ln(999050/13050)}{k}\\\\&\\approx68.8\\text{ weeks}\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
  },
